Z||000002||terryk||06-29-2001||11:42 AM||||On the ALDL connector, I believe the orange wire is a direct feed to the fuel pump. Jumper 12V to it and the pump should run. <P>Assuming the ECM is commanding the pump relay (on the left side of the engine compartment on the firewall), the relay could be bad. Also, C210 (clear connector under the console could be dirty (very unlikely).<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000003||cowans||06-29-2001||11:54 AM||||If you have a V6, the oil pressure switch has 3 wires. Jumper 2 of the 3 wires(not the tan/brown wire, I believe center in cap connecter)...this should power your fuel pump. This was a secondary circuit that Pontiac designed to power your fuel pump if there was enough oil pressure.<BR>Sandy||||reg||1
